jobs.description:
Our client is a rapidly growing international company operating in a highly innovative and industrial environment. Following significant growth and ambitious development projects, the Finance team continues to expand and is looking for a Senior Accountant to strengthen its operations.

Jobomschrijving

Reporting directly to the Head of Finance, you will join a growing finance team and play a key role in ensuring the reliability of the accounting function for the group's main Belgian entities.

Your responsibilities will include:

• Managing the full accounting cycle from A to Z for the group's key Belgian entities;
• Participating in monthly, quarterly, and annual closings in compliance with Belgian GAAP;
• Preparing reconciliations, accruals, provisions, and financial reporting schedules;
• Supporting audit processes and ensuring the accuracy and integrity of financial information;
• Collaborating closely with Business Controllers and operational teams in a project-driven environment;
• Contributing to the implementation and optimisation of accounting processes, controls, and reporting tools;
• Supporting consolidation and group reporting activities when required;
• Acting as a key finance partner in a fast-growing organisation undergoing continuous transformation;

• Bachelor's or Master's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field;
• Several years of accounting experience, ideally gained within an international, industrial, project-based, or fast-growing environment;
• Strong knowledge of Belgian GAAP is essential;
• Experience managing accounting activities independently and operating in a dynamic environment;
• Comfortable working with evolving processes and taking ownership of responsibilities;
• Strong analytical skills and attention to detail;
• Proactive, hands-on, and solution-oriented mindset;
• Fluent in French and/or English;

Are you looking for a temporary job as a packer and do you enjoy working with precision? We are looking for a motivated packer to join the team at an international company based in Willebroek until the end of December 2026.

As a packer, you’ll be responsible for unpacking, labelling and repackaging cassettes and housings. You’ll apply the correct labels to the product and the outer box and ensure that everything is repackaged correctly and carefully.

You will mainly carry out manual and repetitive packing tasks at a workstation. To add variety, you will occasionally swap tasks with your colleagues. You will work in a small team of fewer than ten people, where teamwork and precision are key.

You will start with day shifts from 9.00 am to 5.00 pm, and in time this may change to shifts from 6.00 am to 2.00 pm and 12.00 pm to 8.00 pm.

What do we expect from our packers?

• You have a good command of English, both spoken and written;

• You are fully available until the end of December 2026, with no planned holidays;

• You are flexible regarding working hours and are happy to carry out manual and repetitive packing work;

• Experience as a packer or packaging assistant is an advantage;

• You work accurately and are a good team player.
